nodecode-clack is a rewrite of adroidian's adroidian/clack:

  https://github.com/adroidian/clack
  commit a965b33051d35bcef1dd3fa15255d34aacdba99a
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Aaron Kasten (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the nine tools of the plugin's `plugins/hermes-clack` — whoami,
peers, send, poll, reconcile, ack, invite, join and accept — against the same
relay protocol and the same local posture. What a user gets is unchanged: one
Ed25519 seed that signs every request and, converted through RFC 7748, opens
the X25519 + ChaCha20-Poly1305 envelopes peers send; the relay pinned by a
fresh RSA-2048 challenge before any token or body leaves; one pending outbox
with its receipt read back; a delivery journal written before any
acknowledgement; a quarantine for messages that arrive plaintext or
unreadable; and a join that stays pending until a separate accept. The Python
is Common Lisp here: nlk:http for the exchanges, one section declaration for
the five settings the plugin read from config.yaml, and plist schemas for the
tools whose JSON the plugin wrote by hand. Ironclad carries the curve
arithmetic and the two SHA digests; ChaCha20, Poly1305, HKDF-SHA256,
HMAC-SHA256 and the RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 pin check are written out in
crypto.lisp and envelope.lisp, readable line for line, as the plugin carried
them in vendor/e2ee.py.

Left out, and why: the bundled skill is the manual topic (help :clack) rather
than a skill file, which is how this harness hands the model its etiquette.
The cross-process fcntl lock on the state directory is one in-process lock
(the cell's own), since one image holds the directory. The plugin's
per-file symlink, hardlink, owner and permission scrutiny on every read is
narrowed to owner-only atomic writes under the cell's home. Its HTTP layer
distinguished rejected sends from transport failures to decide what to keep in
the outbox; here any non-2xx answer keeps the outbox and names
clack_reconcile, which is the same instruction in fewer states. The
redirect-free opener is nlk:http's (which follows at most five redirects), so
the origin pin, not the transport, is what a redirect cannot move. The demo,
the test suite and the relay itself stay in the original repository.
